.TH VIPER4LINUX 1 "November 2026" "ViPER4Linux-RE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viper4linux \- launch the ViPER4Linux-RE PipeWire backend and Qt6 GUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viper4linux
.RI [ --fingerprint ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the matching ViPER4Linux-RE PipeWire filter-chain backend if needed,
then launches the Qt6 GUI. A compatible running backend is reused. If an older
marked ViPER backend is present, the launcher attempts to replace only that
instance; it does not restart PipeWire itself. Quit GUI leaves backend audio
processing running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Display available launcher options and exit without starting the backend.
.TP
.B --fingerprint
Print the fingerprint of the installed DSP binary, controller and PipeWire
routing configuration; do not launch the backend or GUI. The launcher uses
this fingerprint to reuse a compatible running instance or to replace its
own older or mismatched instance. It does not terminate unrelated PipeWire
clients.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ViPERforLinux/ViPERClean.conf
Current effect settings and UI preferences (usual location under ~/.config).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/viper4linux/presets/
Named effect presets (usual location under ~/.local/share).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/viper4linux/IRS/
Convolver impulse-response files.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/viper4linux/VDC/
ViPER-DDC profile files.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/viper4linux/backend.log
Backend startup diagnostics (usual location under ~/.local/state).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/viper4linux-re.desktop
Optional user-session autostart created by the GUI.
.SH NOTES
Window/tray behavior and named presets are configured in the GUI.
The backend's virtual sink and routing are PipeWire-specific; audio effects
may continue after the GUI is closed. Start at a safe listening volume.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR v4l-cli (1),
.BR viper4linux-ctl (1)
